# Testing

## Where tests live

- Behavior tests live in the **program that owns the behavior** (`programs/editor|explorer|terminal`).
- Shared helpers belong in `packages/` or a top-level `tests/` — not copied into all three programs.
- Do not add a third test runner. Use Vitest and Playwright only.

## Configs (already in the tree)

- `programs/<name>/src-tauri/configs/vitest.config.ts`
- `programs/<name>/src-tauri/configs/playwright.config.ts`
- `programs/<name>/src-tauri/configs/typescript/tsconfig.test.json`

## Constraints

- Configs and `package.json` scripts are empty until filled. Do not invent runners that are not in those files.
- Prefer `node` over bash. Agent shell is PowerShell.
- Do not complete empty test scaffolding unless the task needs a test.
